            <ArticleTitle>Solitary fibrous tumors of the spine: a pediatric case report with a comprehensive review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-348</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3171/2016.10.PEDS16279</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Solitary fibrous tumors of the spine are rare lesions. Their description in the literature is limited to case reports and small case series. While generally benign lesions, they can recur and occasionally occur as malignancies. Here the authors present the case of a 10-year-old boy, the youngest patient and first preadolescent reported thus far, with this condition. In addition, they perform a comprehensive review of all previously published cases of spinal solitary fibrous tumors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
